  m_Name: 1963
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Merger with Malaysia and Rising Tensions 1963 '
  info: "In a bid to secure economic stability and create a common market, Singapore
    joins the Federation of Malaysia alongside Malaya, Sabah, and Sarawak. However,
    tensions arise over policies favoring ethnic Malays and disputes over political
    representation. Racial riots break out in 1964, straining the relationship between
    Singapore and the central government in Kuala Lumpur. The merger proves untenable,
    leading to Singapore\u2019s separation.  "
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 58af6bf9173604169b57d964c59ee1f1, type: 3}
